From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:13:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] input: share raw gamepad input

Exclusive grabs prevent other consumers, such as Waydroid, from reading raw
gamepad events. Release eligible sources only after host hiding is applied
and verified, retaining the grab on failure so the virtual controller keeps
working.

Detect eligibility from kernel capabilities because hiding changes udev
classification. Generate INPUTPLUMBER_SHARED_GAMEPAD=1 and host input filtering
before uaccess is queued, without profile overrides. Exclude system controls
and root-hidden sources.

Eligible gamepads remain hidden even with passthrough: true. Other
gamepad-driver sources retain upstream's exclusive grab.
